.IX Title "Lucy::Highlight::Highlighter 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Highlight::Highlighter 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Highlight::Highlighter \- Create and highlight excerpts.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 10
\&    my $highlighter = Lucy::Highlight::Highlighter\->new(
\&        searcher => $searcher,
\&        query    => $query,
\&        field    => \*(Aqbody\*(Aq
\&    );
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits( query => $query );
\&    while ( my $hit = $hits\->next ) {
\&        my $excerpt = $highlighter\->create_excerpt($hit);
\&        ...
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The Highlighter can be used to select relevant snippets from a document,
and to surround search terms with highlighting tags.  It handles both stems
and phrases correctly and efficiently, using special-purpose data generated
at index-time.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 6
\&    my $highlighter = Lucy::Highlight::Highlighter\->new(
\&        searcher       => $searcher,    # required
\&        query          => $query,       # required
\&        field          => \*(Aqcontent\*(Aq,    # required
\&        excerpt_length => 150,          # default: 200
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new Highlighter.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsearcher\fR \- An object which inherits from
Searcher, such as an
IndexSearcher.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBquery\fR \- Query object or a query string.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBfield\fR \- The name of the field from which to draw the excerpt.  The
field must marked as be \f(CW\*(C`highlightable\*(C'\fR (see
FieldType).
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBexcerpt_length\fR \- Maximum length of the excerpt, in characters.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS create_excerpt
.IX Subsection "create_excerpt"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $highlighter\->create_excerpt($hit_doc);
.Ve
.PP
Take a HitDoc object and return a highlighted excerpt as a string if
the HitDoc has a value for the specified \f(CW\*(C`field\*(C'\fR.
.SS encode
.IX Subsection "encode"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $highlighter\->encode($text);
.Ve
.PP
Encode text with HTML entities. This method is called internally by
\&\fBcreate_excerpt()\fR for each text fragment when assembling an excerpt.  A
subclass can override this if the text should be encoded differently or
not at all.
.SS highlight
.IX Subsection "highlight"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $highlighter\->highlight($text);
.Ve
.PP
Highlight a small section of text.  By default, prepends pre-tag and
appends post-tag.  This method is called internally by \fBcreate_excerpt()\fR
when assembling an excerpt.
.SS set_pre_tag
.IX Subsection "set_pre_tag"
.Vb 1
\&    $highlighter\->set_pre_tag($pre_tag);
.Ve
.PP
Setter.  The default value is “<strong>”.
.SS set_post_tag
.IX Subsection "set_post_tag"
.Vb 1
\&    $highlighter\->set_post_tag($post_tag);
.Ve
.PP
Setter.  The default value is “</strong>”.
.SS get_pre_tag
.IX Subsection "get_pre_tag"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $highlighter\->get_pre_tag();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor.
.SS get_post_tag
.IX Subsection "get_post_tag"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $highlighter\->get_post_tag();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor.
.SS get_field
.IX Subsection "get_field"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $highlighter\->get_field();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor.
.SS get_excerpt_length
.IX Subsection "get_excerpt_length"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $highlighter\->get_excerpt_length();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor.
.SS get_searcher
.IX Subsection "get_searcher"
.Vb 1
\&    my $searcher = $highlighter\->get_searcher();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor.
.SS get_query
.IX Subsection "get_query"
.Vb 1
\&    my $query = $highlighter\->get_query();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor.
.SS get_compiler
.IX Subsection "get_compiler"
.Vb 1
\&    my $compiler = $highlighter\->get_compiler();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for the Lucy::Search::Compiler object derived from
\&\f(CW\*(C`query\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`searcher\*(C'\fR.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Highlight::Highlighter isa Clownfish::Obj.
